@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: describe sbx resource defaults, then define a blank-slate proveo capacity model for about four agents
' covers: internal/sbx/limits.go
' covers: internal/sbx/sbx.go
' covers: internal/run/run.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/memory_evidence_test.go
' covers: e2e/capacity_test.go
' current evidence: _spec/minimum_requirements.puml
' related lifecycle: _spec/internal/sbx/kit-lifecycle.puml
' status: current defaults measured on sbx v0.42.x; proveo capacity manager proposed 2026-09-17
title Resource management — sbx defaults first;\nthen a four-agent proveo capacity model

package "CURRENT — sbx owns each guest independently" as CURRENT {
  node "host\nRAM · logical CPUs" as HOST <<host>>
  component "sbx sandbox A\n**50% host RAM, fixed at boot**\n**all host CPUs**\n**no swap**" as SBXA <<cloud>>
  component "sbx sandbox B\nsame independent defaults" as SBXB <<cloud>>
  component "sbx sandbox C\nsame independent defaults" as SBXC <<cloud>>
  component "sbx sandbox D\nsame independent defaults" as SBXD <<cloud>>
  component "agent + Kit startup + nested Docker\nshare one guest budget" as LOAD <<app>>
  component "OOM cliff\nprocess cannot fork · guest/session stops" as OOM <<error>>

  HOST ARROW_MAIN SBXA
  HOST ARROW_MAIN SBXB
  HOST ARROW_MAIN SBXC
  HOST ARROW_MAIN SBXD
  SBXA ARROW_MAIN LOAD
  LOAD ARROW_ERROR OOM
}

package "BLANK SLATE — proveo manages host capacity" as FUTURE {
  component "1 · discover host capacity\nRAM · CPUs · existing proveo leases" as DISCOVER <<app>>
  component "2 · reserve host headroom\nnever offer 100% to guests" as RESERVE <<app>>
  database "host-wide lease ledger\nsandbox · profile · RAM · CPUs · phase" as LEDGER <<db>>
  component "3 · classify the requested run\nlite · standard · heavy · explicit" as PROFILE <<app>>
  component "4 · admission decision" as ADMIT <<choice>>
  queue "wait with reason\nand estimated requirement" as WAIT
  component "5 · prepare before attach\nrestore · dependencies · wiring" as PREPARE <<async>>
  component "6 · attach the agent\nonly after preparation completes" as ATTACH <<app>>
  component "7 · observe and account\npeak · OOM · duration · release" as OBSERVE <<app>>

  DISCOVER ARROW_MAIN RESERVE
  RESERVE ARROW_MAIN LEDGER : allocatable pool
  PROFILE ARROW_MAIN ADMIT : requested fixed share
  LEDGER ARROW_MAIN ADMIT : active reservations
  ADMIT ARROW_MAIN PREPARE : enough unleased capacity
  ADMIT ARROW_OPTIONAL WAIT : otherwise
  WAIT ARROW_MAIN ADMIT : lease released
  PREPARE ARROW_MAIN ATTACH : dispatcher complete
  ATTACH ARROW_MAIN OBSERVE
  OBSERVE ARROW_MAIN LEDGER : release + measured peak
  OBSERVE ARROW_OPTIONAL PROFILE : recommend a safer class next run
}

cloud "FUTURE sbx capability\nminimum reservation · balloon/reclaim · maximum cap" as ELASTIC
CURRENT ARROW_OPTIONAL FUTURE : replace independent guesses\nwith one host decision
FUTURE ARROW_OPTIONAL ELASTIC : true on-demand memory requires\nhypervisor + guest support

note top of CURRENT
  **The simple default.** With no ""-m"", sbx
  gives each sandbox half of host RAM. It gives
  each every CPU. RAM is fixed for that guest;
  neither proveo nor sbx rebalances it later.
end note

note bottom of OOM
  **There is no elastic minimum.** The guest has
  no swap, ballooning, free-page reporting or
  hot-resize. A ""--memory"" value is both boot
  size and ceiling, not an on-demand reservation.
end note

note bottom of SBXD
  **Defaults do not compose.** Four independent
  sandboxes each advertising 50% describe 200%
  of host RAM. sbx does not reserve host headroom
  or arbitrate across proveo processes.
end note

note right of LOAD
  **The peak overlaps today.** sbx attaches the
  agent before Kit startup completes. Cursor,
  dependency downloads and nested Docker can
  consume the same fixed pool simultaneously.
end note

note right of LEDGER
  **A declaration is not coordination.** An
  environment variable in one shell cannot see
  runs from another. The ledger needs leases,
  owner liveness and stale-lease recovery.
end note

note bottom of PROFILE
  **Profiles are admission units, not promises.**
  Initial sizes are hypotheses. Replace them with
  measured p95 working sets plus margin, separated
  by harness and capabilities.
end note

note bottom of PREPARE
  **Remove the avoidable peak.** Create and seed
  first, wait on the dispatcher's completion, then
  attach the agent. Heavy preparation receives its
  own concurrency gate.
end note

note bottom of WAIT
  **Queue instead of kill.** A fifth run, or a
  heavy run on a full 16 GiB host, waits and says
  which lease blocks it. ""--no-wait"" fails before
  creating a sandbox.
end note

note bottom of OBSERVE
  **No invisible auto-growth.** A fixed guest
  cannot resize. An OOM records the startup log
  and requested/observed budget, then recommends
  recreation in a larger profile.
end note

note right of ELASTIC
  **The desired contract is min/target/max.** The
  host lends unused pages and reclaims reported
  free pages up to a hard cap. Until sbx exposes
  this, proveo must not pretend a fixed size is
  elastic.
end note

legend bottom
  **Starting profiles — validate with measurements before making these defaults**
  ==
  **lite · 3 GiB** — agent edits/reasons; no browser, nested build or automatic
  dependency provisioning.
  **standard · 6 GiB** — ordinary tests or browser; dependencies prepared before attach.
  **heavy · 10 GiB** — nested Docker, image builds or large language/toolchain setup.
  An explicit ""PROVEO_SBX_MEMORY"" remains an escape hatch, but admission accounts it.
  ==
  **Host matrix for an intention of about four simultaneous agents**
  |= Host RAM |= Reserved for host |= Guest pool |= Honest four-agent posture |
  | 16 GiB | 4 GiB | 12 GiB | 4 lite; or 2 standard; or 1 heavy. Four heavy is rejected. |
  | 32 GiB | 6 GiB | 26 GiB | 4 standard with 2 GiB pool slack; or 2 heavy. |
  | 48 GiB | 8 GiB | 40 GiB | 4 heavy at 10 GiB each. |
  Profiles mix by ordinary bin packing; the rows are examples, not separate modes.
  ==
  **CPU policy** — CPU time is schedulable, unlike RAM. For target concurrency N,
  cap each guest near ""ceil(2 × logical CPUs / N)"", bounded to 2…8 vCPUs, so
  aggregate entitlement may oversubscribe about 2× while idle agents cost little.
  Explicit CPU overrides enter the same ledger.
  ==
  **Meaning of "four agents".** Four live lite agents can fit on 16 GiB only by
  excluding heavyweight capabilities from those 3 GiB guests. proveo must never market
  four arbitrary agents on every host: a profile that can build containers is a
  materially different reservation from one that edits text.
  ==
  **Required CLI surface**
  * ""proveo capacity"" — total, reserve, leases, queue and measured peaks.
  * ""proveo run --resource-profile auto|lite|standard|heavy"".
  * ""proveo run --concurrency-target 4"" — policy input, not proof of capacity.
  * ""proveo clean"" — releases only dead leases; a live sandbox keeps its reservation.
end legend
@enduml
